WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:09.223
Each meter answers a question. The peak meter says whether the signal will clip; the RMS meter says how much energy it has and comes close to loudness.

2
00:00:09.608 --> 00:00:18.262
A short hit raises the peak a lot and the RMS only a little; a sustained note does the opposite. That is why one meter is not enough: you look at both.

3
00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:30.348
To compare two signals you must use the same analysis window: a 300 millisecond RMS and a 10 millisecond one give different numbers for the same sound.

4
00:00:31.046 --> 00:00:37.541
Rule of thumb: the peak for headroom, the RMS for loudness and the spectrum for timbre and noise.
